---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import MadeByKaj from '../../components/MadeByKaj.astro';
const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const materials = [
	{ kind: 'Data access, analysis & views', title: 'Make a star map or a stellar investigation.', text: 'SkyKit offers focused packages for working with astronomical data, drawing maps and diagrams, and composing interactive views.', label: 'Start the SkyKit lessons', href: `${basePath}learn-build/skykit/` },
	{ kind: 'Worlds & motion', title: 'Work with a Solar System experience.', text: 'Pas de Géant brings terrain, scale, planetary positions, and satellite layers into a WebXR application. Its guide covers local setup and a desktop fallback.', label: 'Read the Pas de Géant app guide', href: 'https://github.com/Found-in-Space/pas-de-geant/blob/main/apps/pas-de-geant/README.md' },
	{ kind: 'Eclipse models', title: 'Build with a prediction.', text: 'Shadowline provides eclipse geometry and local circumstances, with map exports and an astronomical provider. It is an early alpha; read the model and validation notes.', label: 'Use the Shadowline example', href: 'https://github.com/Found-in-Space/shadowline#run-an-example' },
	{ kind: 'Data & provenance', title: 'Start from reusable scientific material.', text: 'Use a small star-data query or inspect versioned catalogue publications. The pipeline and spatial packaging tools document how the stellar dataset is made.', label: 'Open the star-data overview', href: `${basePath}build/star-data/` },
	{ kind: 'Authoring', title: 'Compose a journey through a scene.', text: 'SkyKit Studio supports authoring, previewing, editing, retiming, and exporting astronomical journeys. Start with its setup instructions and editor examples.', label: 'Explore SkyKit Studio', href: 'https://github.com/Found-in-Space/skykit-studio' },
	{ kind: 'Interaction', title: 'Give an experience its own tools.', text: 'Touch OS supplies interactive panels and surfaces for 3D scenes. Reuse it for a virtual instrument, a control panel, or another setting beyond astronomy.', label: 'Explore Touch OS', href: 'https://github.com/Found-in-Space/touch-os' },
];
---

<Layout title="Build | Found in Space" description="Make your own investigation, lesson or experience with reusable scientific data, models, components and authoring tools from Found in Space.">
	<SiteHeader section="Build" />
	<main class="page">
		<header class="hero hub-hero">
			<p class="eyebrow">Build</p><h1>Use the materials. Make something yours.</h1>
			<p class="lede">Create an investigation, adapt a teaching activity, compose a journey, or build an application.
				Data, models, components, and authoring tools are part of Found in Space’s purpose.</p>
		</header>
		<section class="hub-section" aria-labelledby="start-title">
			<h2 id="start-title">Choose a starting point.</h2>
			<div class="section-grid section-grid--three">
				<article class="panel destination-card"><p class="panel__eyebrow">Without writing code</p><h3>Make an activity.</h3><p>Choose a viewpoint, compare two cases, or turn a question into a discussion or investigation using an existing experience.</p><div class="destination-card__links"><a class="link--gold" href={`${basePath}teach/`}>Adapt a teaching prompt →</a></div></article>
				<article class="panel destination-card"><p class="panel__eyebrow">A little data or code</p><h3>Make a small first version.</h3><p>Use a bright-star sample for a chart or notebook, or follow a live SkyKit lesson to build a browser view.</p><div class="destination-card__links"><a class="link--gold" href={`${basePath}build/download-the-star-data/`}>Create a starter sample →</a><a class="link--gold" href={`${basePath}learn-build/skykit/`}>Try a live coding lesson →</a></div></article>
				<article class="panel destination-card"><p class="panel__eyebrow">Components & source</p><h3>Find the piece you need.</h3><p>Choose a focused tool or model and follow its setup guide. The developer project map explains how the repositories fit together.</p><div class="destination-card__links"><a class="link--gold" href="https://github.com/Found-in-Space/.github/blob/main/docs/projects.md">Open the developer project map →</a></div></article>
			</div>
		</section>
		<section class="hub-section" aria-labelledby="materials-title">
			<h2 id="materials-title">Tools and materials to build with.</h2>
			<p>Setup and release maturity vary by project. Each linked guide explains what is available and what you need to use it.</p>
			<div class="section-grid section-grid--two">
				{materials.map((item) => <article class="panel destination-card"><p class="panel__eyebrow">{item.kind}</p><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.text}</p><div class="destination-card__links"><a class="link--gold" href={item.href}>{item.label} →</a></div></article>)}
			</div>
			<p>Also taking shape: <a class="link--gold" href={`${basePath}projects/music/`}>Aeolian Measure</a>, for musical creation with measurements. It is in private development; its tools are not yet public.</p>
		</section>
		<section class="hub-note prose">
			<h2>Keep meaning with what you make.</h2>
			<p>Carry sources, units, assumptions, uncertainty, and representation choices into your work.
				Keep observations, inferred values, predictions, and artistic mappings distinguishable.
				Check each dataset’s and package’s licence and attribution requirements.</p>
			<p>For a deeper starting point, see the <a href="https://github.com/Found-in-Space/catalogs">catalogue publications</a>,
				the <a href="https://github.com/Found-in-Space/.github/blob/main/docs/data-and-models.md">data and model guidance</a>,
				or the <a href="https://github.com/Found-in-Space/.github/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">contribution guide</a>.</p>
		</section>
		<MadeByKaj />
	</main>
</Layout>
